WARNING:src.dataset:Input exceeds max_length limit: <s>and yeah oh yeah this is this is um well yeah up here in in in Rochester winter usually doesn't you know spring comes about this time March or April and um this was sort of unexpected it had actually been pretty fairly nice you know in the in the forties and um it had even been in the uh in the in the low fifties a couple of days in a row and then they actually they predicted it they said well we're going to have an ice storm coming up and then no one knew how bad it was going to be and it came in and in one night it basically destroyed it destroyed approximately one third of all the vegetation in um in like the three county area by us and about half the city owned trees in the city of Rochester are destroyed um we had i uh um my wife and i own our own home and we have a very big willow tree in our backyard that um that ninety percent of which came down in one night things like that it was a it it definitely is very um it was it was it wasn't supposed to be as bad they they have i i guess apparently you know ice storms here occasionally but never anything this bad this late in the seaso?<mask>, we had this storm come out of nowhere that was really not expected recently and it destroyed one of our trees and caused damage.</s>
